# NavBar sticky chrome

## Requirement

Pages with app chrome must keep `@podverse/ui` **NavBar** visible while the user scrolls. No page with a navbar is an exception (including `/embed` demo index).

## Implementation (do not regress)

- **NavBar** (`NavBar.module.scss`): `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100` on both management and web appearances. This keeps the bar visible when `#page-wrapper` or the document scrolls.
- **Do not** set `#page-wrapper` to `overflow: hidden` unless every main-content path has a working inner scroll container — that clips long pages (e.g. `/embed` demo).
- **Web inner scroll**: `#mainOuterWrapper` (`MainPageScaffold`) may also scroll on shorter pages; keep `min-height: 0` there so flex layout can shrink the scroll region when `#page-wrapper` does not scroll.
- **Embed iframe routes** (`/embed/*` except `/embed`): remain chromeless via `isEmbedPathname` — no navbar there by design.

## When changing layout

- Do not move scroll from `#mainOuterWrapper` without updating `apps/web/src/utils/scroll.ts` and scroll-restore callers.
- Prefer sticky NavBar over clipping `#page-wrapper` when fixing navbar visibility on long pages.
